{"abstract":"The Arctic–Boreal Zone is rapidly warming, impacting its large soil carbon stocks. Here we use a new compilation of terrestrial ecosystem CO2 fluxes, geospatial datasets and random forest models to show that although the Arctic–Boreal Zone was overall an increasing terrestrial CO2 sink from 2001 to 2020 (mean ± standard deviation in net ecosystem exchange, −548 ± 140 Tg C yr−1; trend, −14 Tg C yr−1; P < 0.001), more than 30% of the region was a net CO2 source. Tundra regions may have already started to function on average as CO2 sources, demonstrating a shift in carbon dynamics. When fire emissions are factored in, the increasing Arctic–Boreal Zone sink is no longer statistically significant (budget, −319 ± 140 Tg C yr−1; trend, −9 Tg C yr−1), and the permafrost region becomes CO2 neutral (budget, −24 ± 123 Tg C yr−1; trend, −3 Tg C yr−1), underscoring the importance of fire in this region.","author_count":63,"contributors":["Virkkala, Anna Maria","Rogers, Brendan M.","Watts, Jennifer D.","Arndt, Kyle A.","Potter, Stefano","Wargowsky, Isabel","Schuur, Edward A.G.","See, Craig R.","Mauritz, Marguerite","Boike, Julia","Bret-Harte, M. Syndonia","Burke, Eleanor J.","Burrell, Arden","Chae, Namyi","Chatterjee, Abhishek","Chevallier, Frederic","Christensen, Torben R.","Commane, Roisin","Dolman, Han","Edgar, Colin W.","Elberling, Bo","Emmerton, Craig A.","Euskirchen, Eugenie S.","Feng, Liang","Göckede, Mathias","Grelle, Achim","Helbig, Manuel","Holl, David","Järveoja, Järvi","Karsanaev, Sergey V.","Kobayashi, Hideki","Kutzbach, Lars","Liu, Junjie","Luijkx, Ingrid T.","López-Blanco, Efrén","Lunneberg, Kyle","Mammarella, Ivan","Marushchak, Maija E.","Mastepanov, Mikhail","Matsuura, Yojiro","Maximov, Trofim C.","Merbold, Lutz","Meyer, Gesa","Nilsson, Mats B.","Niwa, Yosuke","Oechel, Walter","Palmer, Paul I.","Park, Sang Jong","Parmentier, Frans Jan W.","Peichl, Matthias","Peters, Wouter","Petrov, Roman","Quinton, William","Rödenbeck, Christian","Sachs, Torsten","Schulze, Christopher","Sonnentag, Oliver","St. Louis, Vincent L.","Tuittila, Eeva Stiina","Ueyama, Masahito","Varlagin, Andrej","Zona, Donatella","Natali, Susan M."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-793268"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Virkkala, Anna Maria"],"country":["Canada","Finland","France","Germany","Greenland","Japan","Netherlands","Norway","Russia","South Korea","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Agroscope","Alfred Wegener Institute - Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research","Alfred Wegener Institute for Polar and Marine Research (Helmholz)","All Global Affiliations","California Institute of Technology","Cold Regions Research Centre","Columbia University","Dalhousie University","Environment Canada","Environment and Climate Change Canada","Forestry and Forest Products Research Institute","German Research Center for Geosciences (GFZ)","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Helmholtz Centre Potsdam - German Research Centre for Geosciences","Humboldt University of Berlin","Japan Agency for Marine-Earth Science and Technology","Korea Institute of Ocean Science & Technology","Korea Polar Research Institute","Korea University","Linnaeus University","Max Planck Institute for Biogeochemistry","Met Office","Met Office Hadley Centre","Meteorological Research Institute","National Institute for Environmental Studies of Japan","Northern Arizona University","Osaka Metropolitan University","Paris-Saclay University","RAS - Institute for Biological Problems of Cryolithozone, Siberian Branch","RAS - Siberian Branch","Royal Netherlands Institute for Sea Research - NIOZ","Russian Academy of Sciences","San Diego State University","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","Technical University of Braunschweig","United States Army Research Laboratory","Universite Paris-Saclay","University of Alaska Fairbanks","University of Alberta","University of Eastern Finland","University of Edinburgh","University of Groningen","University of Hamburg","University of Helsinki","University of Montreal","University of Oslo","University of Oulu","University of Texas at El Paso","VU University Amsterdam","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","Wageningen University & Research","Woodwell Climate Research Center","Woodwell Climate Research Center, Inc."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wildfires offset the increasing but spatially heterogeneous arctic boreal co sub 000000000002 sub uptake","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41558-024-02234-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-793268","identifier":[{"id":"85217262664","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5f67fcd5-214a-452e-9a25-f6cf9b91effa","ku-6a82b49b-1010-4fac-a891-a99bc095bb2c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E5172E0F3AE566F7AC4D49F9C2F87111"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41558-024-02234-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/430035939/Wildfires_offset_the_increasing_but_spatially_heterogeneous_Arctic_boreal_CO2_uptake.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"woodwell climate research center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Woodwell Climate Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"woodwell climate research center inc","loc":["United States","America, North",