{"abstract":"For the past decade, temporal annotation has been sparse: only a small portion of event pairs in a text was annotated. We present NarrativeTime, the first timeline-based annotation framework that achieves full coverage of all possible TLINKs. To compare with the previous SOTA in dense temporal annotation, we perform full re-annotation of the classic TimeBankDense corpus (American English), which shows comparable agreement with a signigicant increase in density. We contribute TimeBankNT corpus (with each text fully annotated by two expert annotators), extensive annotation guidelines, open-source tools for annotation and conversion to TimeML format, and baseline results.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Karpinska, Marzena","Gupta, Ankita","Lialin, Vladislav","Smelkov, Gregory","Rumshisky, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759421"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["Temporal Annotation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"narrativetime dense temporal annotation on a timeline","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106515396/2024.lrec-main.1054.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759421","identifier":[{"id":"85195912978","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c5f84d5a-5f08-4573-8faf-228091262516"],"keyword":["NarrativeTime","TLINKs","Temporal annotation","TimeBankNT","TimeML"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AC292B0FC98267B1B3D7489277F89A56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106515396/2024.lrec-main.1054.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marzena","key":"karpinskapau","last":"Karpinska","name":"Karpinska, Marzena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ankita","key":"guptapau","last":"Gupta","name":"Gupta, Ankita","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vladislav","key":"lialinpau","last":"Lialin","name":"Lialin, Vladislav","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregory","key":"smelkovpau","last":"Smelkov","name":"Smelkov, Gregory","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rumshiskypau","last":"Rumshisky","name":"Rumshisky, Anna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicoletta","key":"calzolaripedh","last":"Calzolari","name":"Calzolari, Nicoletta","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Min-Yen","key":"kanpedh","last":"Kan","name":"Kan, Min-Yen","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Veronique","key":"hostepedh","last":"Hoste","name":"Hoste, Veronique","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alessandro","key":"lencipedh","last":"Lenci","name":"Lenci, Alessandro","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sakriani","key":"saktipedh","last":"Sakti","name":"Sakti, Sakriani","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nianwen","key":"xuepedh","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Nianwen","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"12053-12073","place":"Torino, Italia","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Joint International Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC-COLING 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c5f84d5a-5f08-4573-8faf-228091262516"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"NarrativeTime: Dense Temporal Annotation on a Timeline","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759421","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Novel methods for sampling and characterizing biodiversity hold great promise for re-evaluating patterns of life across the planet. The sampling of airborne spores with a cyclone sampler, and the sequencing of their DNA, have been suggested as an efficient and well-calibrated tool for surveying fungal diversity across various environments. Here we present data originating from the Global Spore Sampling Project, comprising 2,768 samples collected during two years at 47 outdoor locations across the world. Each sample represents fungal DNA extracted from 24 m3 of air. We applied a conservative bioinformatics pipeline that filtered out sequences that did not show strong evidence of representing a fungal species. The pipeline yielded 27,954 species-level operational taxonomic units (OTUs). Each OTU is accompanied by a probabilistic taxonomic classification, validated through comparison with expert evaluations. To examine the potential of the data for ecological analyses, we partitioned the variation in species distributions into spatial and seasonal components, showing a strong effect of the annual mean temperature on community composition.","author_count":116,"contributors":["Ovaskainen, Otso","Abrego, Nerea","Furneaux, Brendan","Hardwick, Bess","Somervuo, Panu","Palorinne, Isabella","Andrew, Nigel R.","Babiy, Ulyana V.","Bao, Tan","Bazzano, Gisela","Bondarchuk, Svetlana N.","Bonebrake, Timothy C.","Brennan, Georgina L.","Bret-Harte, Syndonia","Bässler, Claus","Cagnolo, Luciano","Cameron, Erin K.","Chapurlat, Elodie","Creer, Simon","D’Acqui, Luigi P.","de Vere, Natasha","Desprez-Loustau, Marie Laure","Dongmo, Michel A.K.","Dyrholm Jacobsen, Ida B.","Fisher, Brian L.","Flores de Jesus, Miguel","Gilbert, Gregory S.","Griffith, Gareth W.","Gritsuk, Anna A.","Gross, Andrin","Grudd, Håkan","Halme, Panu","Hanna, Rachid","Hansen, Jannik","Hansen, Lars Holst","Hegbe, Apollon D.M.T.","Hill, Sarah","Hogg, Ian D.","Hultman, Jenni","Hyde, Kevin D.","Hynson, Nicole A.",