{"abstract":"Much of the recent discourse within the NLP research community has been centered around Large Language Models (LLMs), their functionality and potential -- yet not only do we not have a working definition of LLMs, but much of this discourse relies on claims and assumptions that are worth re-examining. This position paper contributes a definition of LLMs, explicates some of the assumptions made regarding their functionality, and outlines the existing evidence for and against them. We conclude with suggestions for research directions and their framing in future work.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Luccioni, Alexandra Sasha","Rogers, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695261"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hugging Face"],"keyword":["Assumptions","Functionality","Large Language Models","NLP","Research directions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mind your language model fact checking llms and their role in nlp research and practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.07120","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695261","ids":["itu-84a1eb5a-3869-4af1-9388-f1cd8f2174d6"],"keyword":["Large Language Models","NLP","assumptions","functionality","research directions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6DD8F62295C64391804F18B8CB73D50A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.07120","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2308.07120","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"hugging face","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Hugging Face","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandra Sasha","key":"luccionipau","last":"Luccioni","name":"Luccioni, Alexandra Sasha","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"arXiv","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-84a1eb5a-3869-4af1-9388-f1cd8f2174d6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mind Your Language (Model): Fact-Checking LLMs and Their Role in NLP Research and Practice","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695261","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We propose a novel challenge for large language models: ellipsis-dependent reasoning. We define several structures of paired examples, where an ellipsis example is matched to its non-ellipsis counterpart, and a question is posed which requires resolution of the ellipsis. Test results show that the best models perform well on non-elliptical examples but struggle with all but the simplest ellipsis structures.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hardt, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-683023"],"event":{"end":"2023-07-14","place":"Toronto, ca","start":"2023-07-09","title":"The 61st Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ellipsis dependent reasoning a new challenge for large language models","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/96138025/daniel_hardt_ellipsis-dependent_reasoning_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-683023","ids":["cbs-66948743-ec2e-4c99-8b34-8d2db8af7a48"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FEA6DBB2E225C50DF4D8167FE1980093"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/volumes/2023.acl-short/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/96138025/daniel_hardt_ellipsis-dependent_reasoning_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"hardtpau","last":"Hardt","locid":"afd9ce14-fa22-401a-8e3c-964ed4b0eb30","name":"Hardt, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-6041-1475","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"rogerspedh","last":"Rogers","name":"Rogers, Anna","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jordan","key":"boydgraberpedh","last":"Boyd-Graber","name":"Boyd-Graber, Jordan","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Naoaki","key":"okazakipedh","last":"Okazaki","name":"Okazaki, Naoaki","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781959429715"],"pages":"39-47","place":"Stroudsburg","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 61st Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172202787"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-66948743-ec2e-4c99-8b34-8d2db8af7a48"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Ellipsis-dependent Reasoning : A New Challenge for Large Language Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-683023","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We present a summary of the efforts to improve conference peer review that were implemented at ACL'23. This includes work with the goal of improving review quality, clearer workflow and decision support for the area chairs, as well as our efforts to improve paper-reviewer matching for various kinds of non- mainstream NLP work, and improve the overall incentives for all participants of the peer review process. We present analysis of the factors affecting peer review, identify the most problematic issues that the authors complained about, and provide suggestions for the future chairs. We hope that publishing such reports would (a) improve transparency in decision-making, (b) help the people new to the field to understand how the *ACL conferences work, (c) provide useful data for the future chairs and workshop organizers, and also academic work on peer review, and (d) provide useful context for the final program, as a source of information for meta-research on the structure and trajectory of the field of NLP.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Karpinska, Marzena","Boyd-Graber, Jordan","Okazaki, Naoaki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695254"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tokyo Institute of Technology","University of Maryland","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["ACL 23","Conference Management","Decision support","Incentives","Meta research","NLP","Peer Review Matching","Peer review","Review Quality","Transparency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"program chairs report on peer review at acl 000000002023","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":