{"abstract":"ROOTS is a 1.6TB multilingual text corpus developed for the training of BLOOM, currently the largest language model explicitly accompanied by commensurate data governance efforts. In continuation of these efforts, we present the ROOTS Search Tool: a search engine over the entire ROOTS corpus offering both fuzzy and exact search capabilities. ROOTS is the largest corpus to date that can be investigated this way. The ROOTS Search Tool is open-sourced and available on Hugging Face Spaces: https://huggingface.co/spaces/bigscience-data/roots-search. We describe our implementation and the possible use cases of our tool.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Piktus, Aleksandra","Akiki, Christopher","Villegas, Paulo","Laurençon, Hugo","Dupont, Gérard","Luccioni, Sasha","Jernite, Yacine","Rogers, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695296"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy","Spain","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hugging Face","Leipzig University","Mavenoid","Sapienza University of Rome","ScaDS.AI","Telefonica Research, Madrid"],"keyword":["Data governance","Language Model Training","Multilingual Text Corpus","Open source tool","Search Engine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the roots search tool data transparency for llms","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.acl-demo.29","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695296","identifier":[{"id":"85173514562","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cac34f53-3958-43c5-808f-d4ff52db8f8b"],"keyword":["Data Governance","Language Model Training","Multilingual Text Corpus","Open-Source Tool","Search Engine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-284E92DB086C5DE75959F39A31DFDB1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-demo.29.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.acl-demo.29","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-demo.29","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"sapienza university of rome","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sapienza University of Rome","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"hugging face","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Hugging Face","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"leipzig university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leipzig University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"scads ai","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ScaDS.AI","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"telefonica research madrid","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Telefonica Research, Madrid","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"mavenoid","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Mavenoid","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandra","key":"piktuspau","last":"Piktus","name":"Piktus, Aleksandra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"akikipau","last":"Akiki","name":"Akiki, Christopher","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Paulo","key":"villegaspau","last":"Villegas","name":"Villegas, Paulo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo","key":"laurençonpau","last":"Laurençon","name":"Laurençon, Hugo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Gérard","key":"dupontpau","last":"Dupont","name":"Dupont, Gérard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sasha","key":"luccionipau","last":"Luccioni","name":"Luccioni, Sasha","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yacine","key":"jernitepau","last":"Jernite","name":"Jernite, Yacine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2023.acl-demo.29","pages":"304-314","place":"Toronto, Canada","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 61st Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 3: System Demonstrations)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173514562"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cac34f53-3958-43c5-808f-d4ff52db8f8b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The ROOTS Search Tool: Data Transparency for LLMs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695296","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Coreference resolution is the task of finding expressions that refer to the same entity in a text. Coreference models are generally trained on monolingual annotated data but annotating coreference is expensive and challenging. Hardmeier et al. (2013) have shown that parallel data contains latent anaphoric knowledge, but it has not been explored in end-to-end neural models yet. In this paper, we propose a simple yet effective model to exploit coreference knowledge from parallel data. In addition to the conventional modules learning coreference from annotations, we introduce an unsupervised module to capture cross-lingual coreference knowledge. Our proposed cross-lingual model achieves consistent improvements, up to 1.74 percentage points, on the OntoNotes 5.0 English dataset using 9 different synthetic parallel datasets. These experimental results confirm that parallel data can provide additional coreference knowledge which is beneficial to coreference resolution tasks.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tang, Gongbo","Hardmeier, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712526"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Language and Culture University"],"keyword":["Anaphoric Knowledge","Coreference Knowledge","Coreference Resolution","Cross lingual Coreference","Monolingual Annotated Data","Neural models","OntoNotes 5 0","Parallel Data","Synthetic Datasets","Unsupervised learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parallel data helps neural entity coreference resolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.findings-acl.197","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712526","identifier":[{"id":"85175434823","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-669e4778-b4ea-49eb-a8dc-920fe5722925"],"keyword":["Anaphoric Knowledge","Coreference Knowledge","Coreference Resolution","Cross-lingual Coreference","Monolingual Annotated Data","Neural Models","OntoNotes 5.0","Parallel Data","Synthetic Datasets","Unsupervised Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-40BF75BD02D64A87F4441A1004CF7298"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.findings-acl.197","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.findings-acl.197.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beijing language and culture university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Language and Culture University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gongbo","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Gongbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hardmeierpau","last":"Hardmeier","locid":"9504265d-0046-4e58-b529-256a656c012d","name":"Hardmeier, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-6103-7275","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"rogerspedh","last":"Rogers","name":"Rogers, Anna","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jordan","key":"boydgraberpedh","last":"Boyd-Graber","name":"Boyd-Graber, Jordan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Naoaki","key":"okazakipedh","last":"Okazaki","name":"Okazaki, Naoaki","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2023.findings-acl.197","edition":"2023","eisbn":["9781959429623"],"pages":"3162-3171","place":"Canada","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: ACL 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-669e4778-b4ea-49eb-a8dc-920fe5722925"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parallel Data Helps Neural Entity Coreference Resolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712526","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The objectives of this study were to assess Candida spp. distribution and antifungal resistance of candidaemia across Europe. Isolates were collected as part of the third ECMM Candida European multicentre observational study, conducted from 01 to 07-07-2018 to 31-03-2022. Each centre (maximum number/country determined by population size) included ∼10 consecutive cases. Isolates were referred to central laboratories and identified by morphology and MALDI-TOF, supplemented by ITS-sequencing when needed. EUCAST MICs were determined for five antifungals. fks sequencing was performed for echinocandin resistant isolates. The 399 isolates from 41 centres in 17 countries included C. albicans (47.1%), C. glabrata (22.3%), C. parapsilosis (15.0%), C. tropicalis (6.3%), C. dubliniensis and C. krusei (2.3% each) and other species (4.8%). Austria had the highest C. albicans proportion (77%), Czech Republic, France and UK the highest C. glabrata proportions (25–33%) while Italy and Turkey had the highest C. parapsilosis proportions (24–26%). All isolates were amphotericin B susceptible. Fluconazole resistance was found in 4% C. tropicalis, 12% C. glabrata (from six countries across Europe), 17% C. parapsilosis (from Greece, Italy, and Turkey) and 20% other Candida spp. Four isolates were anidulafungin and micafungin resistant/non-wild-type and five resistant to micafungin only. Three/3 and 2/5 of these were sequenced and harboured fks-alterations including a novel L657W in C. parapsilosis. The epidemiology varied among centres and countries. Acquired echinocandin resistance was rare but included differential susceptibility to anidulafungin and micafungin, and resistant C. parapsilosis. Fluconazole and voriconazole cross-resistance was common in C. glabrata and C. parapsilosis but with different geographical prevalence.","author_count":47,"contributors":["Arendrup, Maiken Cavling","Arikan-Akdagli, Sevtap","Jørgensen, Karin Meinike","Barac, Aleksandra","Steinmann, Jörg","Toscano, Cristina","Arsenijevic, Valentina Arsic","Sartor, Assunta","Lass-Flörl, Cornelia","Hamprecht, Axel","Matos, Tadeja","Rogers, Benedict R.S.","Quiles, Inmaculada","Buil, Jochem","Özenci, Volkan","Krause, Robert","Bassetti, Matteo","Loughlin, Laura","Denis, Blandine","Grancini, Anna","White, P. Lewis","Lagrou, Katrien","Willinger, Birgit","Rautemaa-Richardson, Riina","Hamal, Petr","Ener, Beyza","Unalan-Altintop, Tugce","Evren, Ebru","Hilmioglu-Polat, Suleyha","Oz, Yasemin","Ozyurt, Ozlem Koyuncu","Aydin, Faruk","Růžička, Filip","Meijer, Eelco F.J.","Gangneux, Jean Pierre","Lockhart, Deborah E.A.","Khanna, Nina","Logan, Clare","Scharmann, Ulrike","Desoubeaux, Guillaume","Roilides, Emmanuel","Talento, Alida Fe","van Dijk, Karin","Koehler, Philipp","Salmanton-García, Jon","Cornely, Oliver A.","Hoenigl, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720538"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Czechia","France","Germany","Greece","Ireland","Italy","Netherlands","Portugal","Serbia","Slovenia","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","Turkey","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Akdeniz University","All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Ankara University","Aristotle University of Thessaloniki","Azienda Sanitaria Universitaria del Friuli Centrale","Belfast Health and Social Care Trust","BioTechMed-Graz","Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital","Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Tours","Clinical Center of Serbia","Ege University","Hacettepe University","Hospital São José","IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliera Universitaria San Martino IST - Istituto Nazionale per la Ricerca sul Cancro","IRCCS Fondazione Ca'Granda – Ospedale Maggiore Policlinico - Milano","Innsbruck Medical University","KU Leuven","Karadeniz Technical University","Karolinska Institutet","Klinikum Nurnberg","Masaryk University","Medical University of Graz","Medical University of Vienna","NHS Grampian","Osmangazi University","Palacký University Olomouc","Public Health Wales","Radboud University Nijmegen","Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland","Saint-Louis University Hospital","St. George's University of London","Uludag University","Universidad Autónoma de Madrid","University Hospital Essen","University Hospitals of Leicester NHS Trust","University of Aberdeen","University of Basel","University of Belgrade","University of Cologne","University of Genoa","University of Ljubljana","University of Manchester","University of Oldenburg","Wythenshawe Hospital","École des hautes études en santé publique"],"keyword":["Candida","EUCAST","Echinocandin resistance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"european candidaemia is characterised by notable differential epidemiology and susceptibility pattern results from the ecmm candida iii study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jinf.2023.08.001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720538","identifier":[{"id":"85170210574","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37549695","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6804b452-d740-4692-b94f-be0f81c0ab64"],"keyword":["C. parapsilosis","Candida","EUCAST","Echinocandin resistance","Fks1","Fluconazole resistance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B426FBB1A2D65083C8E00B92489AAF88"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jinf.2023.08.001","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375195106/1_s2.0_S0163445323