nhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a9aaa161-5cfc-42f5-9a30-6b662f98d0c0","ku-08da2630-3d31-4ced-a321-78d73d8c07cb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The ABCflux database : Arctic-boreal CO<sub>2</sub> flux observations and ancillary information aggregated to monthly time steps across terrestrial ecosystems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.08-025044","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Ubiquitin is a small, globular protein that is conjugated to other proteins as a posttranslational event. A palette of small, folded domains recognizes and binds ubiquitin to translate and effectuate this posttranslational signal. Recent computational studies have suggested that protein regions can recognize ubiquitin via a process of folding upon binding. Using peptide binding arrays, bioinformatics, and NMR spectroscopy, we have uncovered a disordered ubiquitin-binding motif that likely remains disordered when bound and thus expands the palette of ubiquitin-binding proteins. We term this motif Disordered Ubiquitin-Binding Motif (DisUBM) and find it to be present in many proteins with known or predicted functions in degradation and transcription. We decompose the determinants of the motif showing it to rely on features of aromatic and negatively charged residues, and less so on distinct sequence positions in line with its disordered nature. We show that the affinity of the motif is low and moldable by the surrounding disordered chain, allowing for an enhanced interaction surface with ubiquitin, whereby the affinity increases ~ tenfold. Further affinity optimization using peptide arrays pushed the affinity into the low micromolar range, but compromised context dependence. Finally, we find that DisUBMs can emerge from unbiased screening of randomized peptide libraries, featuring in de novo cyclic peptides selected to bind ubiquitin chains. We suggest that naturally occurring DisUBMs can recognize ubiquitin as a posttranslational signal to act as affinity enhancers in IDPs that bind to folded and ubiquitylated binding partners.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Dreier, Jesper E.","Prestel, Andreas","da Silva Martins, João Miguel","Brøndum, Sebastian S.","Nielsen, Olaf","Garbers, Anna E.","Suga, Hiroaki","Boomsma, Wouter","Rogers, Joseph M.","Hartmann-Petersen, Rasmus","Kragelund, Birthe B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446666"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The University of Tokyo"],"keyword":["Context","Cyclic peptide","Deep mutational scanning","IDP","NMR","SLiM","UBM","Ubiquitin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a context dependent and disordered ubiquitin binding motif","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00018-022-04486-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446666","identifier":[{"id":"85135979730","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9381478","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35974206","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-58f6c917-5f88-4fd0-bb2b-98ebc5813206"],"keyword":["Context","Cyclic peptide","Deep mutational scanning","IDP","NMR","SLiM","UBM","Ubiquitin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6A5BFE1F8896C97564E2B8CC4BE520D5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00018-022-04486-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/318035962/A_context_dependent_and_disordered_ubiquitin_binding_motif.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Biomolecular Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"jp","key":"the university of tokyo","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"The University of Tokyo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper E.","key":"dreierpau","last":"Dreier","locid":"a0a01a30-3bd9-4616-a01c-b6b6dbe1b7d4","name":"Dreier, Jesper E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"prestelpau","last":"Prestel","locid":"f60090ef-7296-43ef-a98a-713fd09d47fe","name":"Prestel, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"João M.","key":"martinspau","last":"Martins","locid":"2dcb08ec-d44b-4366-bd7d-0f89e75f3e45","name":"da Silva Martins, João Miguel","name_org":"Martins, João M.","orcid":"0000-0003-3053-3775","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian S.","key":"brøndumpau","last":"Brøndum","name":"Brøndum, Sebastian S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olaf","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5fcd7b51-a4f6-4b47-8253-23e652a7a6f5","name":"Nielsen, Olaf","orcid":"0000-0001-7440-5201","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna E.","key":"garberspau","last":"Garbers","locid":"1274ba2f-c404-4b63-baa2-dee4082aa0d0","name":"Garbers, Anna E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hiroaki","key":"sugapau","last":"Suga","name":"Suga, Hiroaki","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wouter","key":"boomsmapau","last":"Boomsma","locid":"2462ed56-4538-4107-80a7-57145db12a08","name":"Boomsma, Wouter","orcid":"0000-0002-8257-3827","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Joseph M.","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"51d6d50f-7190-4439-837c-3798a0fc9caf","name":"Rogers, Joseph M.","orcid":"0000-0002-1313-4089","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hartmannpetersenpau","last":"Hartmann-Petersen","locid":"fea900ee-b167-45e9-af2c-00038ff06862","name":"Hartmann-Petersen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0002-4155-7791","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birthe B.","key":"kragelundpau","last":"Kragelund","locid":"c3a5d42e-5e73-4af3-94f9-22550bb7c499","name":"Kragelund, Birthe B.","orcid":"0000-0002-7454-1761","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35974206"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00018-022-04486-w","issn":["1420682X","14209071"],"issn_org":["1420682X"],"issue":"9","journal":"Cellular and Molecular Life Sciences","paperid":"484","status":"p","title":"Cellular and Molecular Life Sciences","title_org":"Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135979730"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-58f6c917-5f88-4fd0-bb2b-98ebc5813206"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A context-dependent and disordered ubiquitin-binding motif","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446666","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The Global Strategy Lab at York University offers this written submission in response to the current Working Draft of the pandemic instrument (document A/INB/2/3), developed in collaboration with our partners International Centre for Antimicrobial Resistance Solutions (ICARS), International Network for AMR Social Science (INAMRSS), One Health Trust (OHT), and ReAct – Action on Antibiotic Resistance. To enhance the pandemic instrument’s ability to protect the international community from future infectious disease crises, we recommend that the instrument be designed to comprehensively address the full range of pandemic threats. We note with concern that antimicrobial resistance (AMR) has not been adequately included within the scope of the treaty despite being a widely recognized and growing global pandemic.¨ In the submission we also give recommendations on how to include AMR.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Van Katwyk, Susan Rogers","Engslund Krarup, Helle","Laxminarayan, Ramanan","Chandy, Sujith","Mpundu, Morfin","Sjöblom, Anna Karin","Minssen, Timo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-465677"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","OECD"],"country":["Canada","India"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Center for Disease Dynamics","York University Toronto"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"submission to the intergovernmental negotiating body re the need to include amr related provision in the un who pandemic instrument","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-465677","ids":["ku-78ac0c0d-e8b3-4eef-b129-839a28a2c054"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A635F09283A19192357C6E92065C1768"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"york university toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"York University Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"center for disease dynamics","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Center for Disease Dynamics","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, JUR Center for Advanced Studies in Bioscience Innovation Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Susan Rogers","key":"vankatwykpau","last":"Van Katwyk","name":"Van Katwyk, Susan Rogers","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"engslundkraruppau","last":"Engslund Krarup","name":"Engslund Krarup, Helle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ramanan","key":"laxminarayanpau","last":"Laxminarayan","name":"Laxminarayan, Ramanan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sujith","key":"chandypau","last":"Chandy","name":"Chandy, Sujith","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morfin","key":"mpundupau","last":"Mpundu","name":"Mpundu, Morfin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna Karin","key":"sjöblompau","last":"Sjöblom","name":"Sjöblom, Anna Karin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Timo","key":"minssenpau","last":"Minssen","locid":"7ded1eca-75f2-4e95-ab13-4f66cb51ec0b","name":"Minssen, Timo","orcid":"0000-0002-3286-4888","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-78ac0c0d-e8b3-4eef-b129-839a28a2c054"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Submission to the Intergovernmental Negotiating Body; RE: The need to include AMR-related provision in the UN/WHO Pandemic Instrument","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-465677","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"For the past decade, temporal annotation has been sparse: only a small portion of event pairs in a text was annotated. We present NarrativeTime, the first timeline-based annotation framework that achieves full coverage of all possible TLinks. To compare with the previous SOTA in dense temporal annotation, we perform full re-annotation of TimeBankDense corpus, which shows comparable agreement with a significant increase in density. We contribute TimeBankNT corpus (with each text fully annotated by two expert annotators), extensive annotation guidelines, open-source tools for annotation and conversion to TimeML format, baseline results, as well as quantitative and qualitative analysis of inter-annotator agreement.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Karpinska, Marzena","Gupta, Ankita","Lialin, Vladislav","Smelkov, Gregory","Rumshisky, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695276"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["Event Pairs","Inter Annotator Agreement","Temporal Annotation","TimeBankDense Corpus","Timeline Based Annotation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"narrativetime dense temporal annotation on a timeline","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-695276","ids":["itu-ac5a3b03-ee6f-4fdc-ac5b-a5532b729bfa"],"keyword":["Event Pairs","Inter-Annotator Agreement","Temporal Annotation","TimeBankDense Corpus","Timeline-Based Annotation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9CC734C27C84423513BD61E4949FC39C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"univer