{"abstract":"Multiple studies have shown that Transformers are remarkably robust to pruning. Contrary to this received wisdom, we demonstrate that pre-trained Transformer encoders are surprisingly fragile to the removal of a very small number of features in the layer outputs ($","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kovaleva, Olga","Kulshreshtha, Saurabh","Rogers, Anna","Rumshisky, Anna"],"cuid":["S02-099.44-692202"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["Feature pruning","Layer outputs","Model fragility","Pre trained models","Transformers robustness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bert busters outlier dimensions that disrupt transformers","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85115709718","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.44-692202","identifier":[{"id":"85115709718","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3ec033a5-b6aa-4268-8fca-ad93977d6249","ku-8ba37881-dc60-4980-993c-523dc0a45912"],"keyword":["Feature pruning","Layer outputs","Model fragility","Pre-trained models","Transformers robustness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-615635CC03115AB5AEFDF6E86494C87C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, shared expenditure, Social Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olga","key":"kovalevapau","last":"Kovaleva","name":"Kovaleva, Olga","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saurabh","key":"kulshreshthapau","last":"Kulshreshtha","name":"Kulshreshtha, Saurabh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"e8d3de73-eb20-4bda-9f0e-6bf8a7bdac21","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rumshiskypau","last":"Rumshisky","name":"Rumshisky, Anna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2021.findings-acl.300","pages":"3392-3405","place":"Online","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL)","status":"p","title":"Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: ACL-IJCNLP 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115709718"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3ec033a5-b6aa-4268-8fca-ad93977d6249","ku-8ba37881-dc60-4980-993c-523dc0a45912"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"BERT Busters: Outlier Dimensions That Disrupt Transformers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.44-692202","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Breast cancer (BC) risk for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers varies by genetic and familial factors. About 50 common variants have been shown to modify BC risk for mutation carriers. All but three, were identified in general population studies. Other mutation carrier-specific susceptibility variants may exist but studies of mutation carriers have so far been underpowered. We conduct a novel case-only genome-wide association study comparing genotype frequencies between 60,212 general population BC cases and 13,007 cases with BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations. We identify robust novel associations for 2 variants with BC for BRCA1 and 3 for BRCA2 mutation carriers, P < 10−8, at 5 loci, which are not associated with risk in the general population. They include rs60882887 at 11p11.2 where MADD, SP11 and EIF1, genes previously implicated in BC biology, are predicted as potential targets. These findings will contribute towards customising BC polygenic risk scores for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers.","author_count":384,"contributors":["Coignard, Juliette","Lush, Michael","Beesley, Jonathan","O’Mara, Tracy A.","Dennis, Joe","Tyrer, Jonathan P.","Barnes, Daniel R.","McGuffog, Lesley","Leslie, Goska","Bolla, Manjeet K.","Adank, Muriel A.","Agata, Simona","Ahearn, Thomas","Aittomäki, Kristiina","Andrulis, Irene L.","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Arndt, Volker","Arnold, Norbert","Aronson, Kristan J.","Arun, Banu K.","Augustinsson, Annelie","Azzollini, Jacopo","Barrowdale, Daniel","Baynes, Caroline","Becher, Heko","Bermisheva, Marina","Bernstein, Leslie","Białkowska, Katarzyna","Blomqvist, Carl","Bojesen, Stig E.","Bonanni, Bernardo","Borg, Ake","Brauch, Hiltrud","Brenner, Hermann","Burwinkel, Barbara","Buys, Saundra S.","Caldés, Trinidad","Caligo, Maria A.","Campa, Daniele","Carter, Brian D.","Castelao, Jose E.","Chang-Claude, Jenny","Chanock, Stephen J.","Chung, Wendy K.","Claes, Kathleen B.M.","Clarke, Christine","Bertrand, Ophélie","Caputo, Sandrine","Dupré, Anaïs","Le Mentec, Marine","Belotti, Muriel","Birot, Anne Marie","Buecher, Bruno","Fourme, Emmanuelle","Gauthier-Villars, Marion","Golmard, Lisa","Houdayer, Claude","Moncoutier, Virginie","de Pauw, Antoine","Saule, Claire","Sinilnikova, Olga","Mazoyer, Sylvie","Damiola, Francesca","Barjhoux, Laure","Verny-Pierre, Carole","Léone, Mélanie","Boutry-Kryza, Nadia","Calender, Alain","Giraud, Sophie","Caron, Olivier","Guillaud-Bataille, Marine","Bressac-de-Paillerets, Brigitte","Bignon, Yves Jean","Uhrhammer, Nancy","Lasset, Christine","Bonadona, Valérie","Berthet, Pascaline","Vaur, Dominique","Castera, Laurent","Noguchi, Tetsuro","Popovici, Cornel","Sobol, Hagay","Bourdon, Violaine","Noguchi, Tetsuro","Remenieras, Audrey","Noguès, Catherine","Coupier, Isabelle","Pujol, Pascal","Dumont, Aurélie","Révillion, Françoise","Adenis, Claude","Muller, Danièle","Barouk-Simonet, Emmanuelle","Bonnet, Françoise","Bubien, Virginie","Sevenet, Nicolas","Longy, Michel","Toulas, Christine","Guimbaud, Rosine","Gladieff, Laurence","Feillel, Viviane","Leroux, Dominique","Dreyfus, Hélène","Rebischung, Christine","Peysselon, Magalie","Coron, Fanny","Faivre, Laurence","Baurand, Amandine","Jacquot, Caroline","Bertolone, Geoffrey","Lizard, Sarab","Prieur, Fabienne","Lebrun, Marine","Kientz, Caroline","Ferrer, Sandra Fert","Mari, Véronique","Vénat-Bouvet, Laurence","Delnatte, Capucine","Bézieau, Stéphane","Mortemousque, Isabelle","Coulet, Florence","Colas, Chrystelle","Soubrier, Florent","Warcoin, Mathilde","Sokolowska, Johanna","Bronner, Myriam","Collonge-Rame, Marie Agnès","Damette, Alexandre","Gesta, Paul","Lallaoui, Hakima","Chiesa, Jean","Molina-Gomes, Denise","Ingster, Olivier","Gregory, Helen","Miedzybrodzka, Zosia","Morrison, Patrick J.","Ong, Kai ren","Donaldson, Alan","Rogers, Mark T.","Kennedy, M. John","Porteous, Mary E.","Brewer, Carole","Davidson, Rosemarie","Izatt, Louise","Brady, Angela","Barwell, Julian","Adlard, Julian","Foo, Claire","Lalloo, Fiona","Side, Lucy E.","Eason, Jacqueline","Henderson, A