{"abstract":"The recent explosion in question answering research produced a wealth of both factoid RC and commonsense reasoning datasets. Combining them presents a different kind of task: not deciding simply whether information is present in the text, but also whether a confident guess could be made for the missing information. To that end, we present QuAIL, the first reading comprehension dataset (a) to combine textbased, world knowledge and unanswerable questions, and (b) to provide annotation that would enable precise diagnostics of the reasoning strategies by a given QA system. QuAIL contains 15K multi-choice questions for 800 texts in 4 domains (fiction, blogs, political news, and user story texts). Crucially, to solve QuAIL a system would need to handle both general and text-specific questions, impossible to answer from pretraining data. We show that the new benchmark poses substantial challenges to the current state-of-the-art systems, with a 30% drop in accuracy compared to the most similar existing dataset.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Kovaleva, Olga","Downey, Matthew","Rumshisky, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695272"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["Commonsense reasoning","Diagnostic annotation","Multi choice questions","Question answering QA","Reading comprehension dataset"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"getting closer to ai complete question answering a set of prerequisite real tasks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://aaai.org/ojs/index.php/AAAI/article/view/6398","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695272","ids":["itu-9ccafb8e-c7d3-430c-b54c-74ebc40e0826"],"keyword":["Commonsense reasoning","Diagnostic annotation","Multi-choice questions","Question answering (QA)","Reading comprehension dataset"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FAAB208A1CC2018EC16B142AC6527C7B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olga","key":"kovalevapau","last":"Kovaleva","name":"Kovaleva, Olga","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthew","key":"downeypau","last":"Downey","name":"Downey, Matthew","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rumshiskypau","last":"Rumshisky","name":"Rumshisky, Anna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"11","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9ccafb8e-c7d3-430c-b54c-74ebc40e0826"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Getting Closer to AI Complete Question Answering: A Set of Prerequisite Real Tasks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695272","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
