{"abstract":"Transformer-based models have pushed state of the art in many areas of NLP, but our understanding of what is behind their success is still limited. This paper is the first survey of over 150 studies of the popular BERT model. We review the current state of knowledge about how BERT works, what kind of information it learns and how it is represented, common modifications to its training objectives and architecture, the overparameterization issue, and approaches to compression. We then outline directions for future research.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Kovaleva, Olga","Rumshisky, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695236"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["BERT model analysis","Model compression techniques","Neural network overparameterization","Training objective modifications","Transformer based models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a primer in bertology what we know about how bert works","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85098839172","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695236","identifier":[{"id":"85098839172","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-40be91bf-0fd1-449e-9d0d-ac2961bdd112"],"keyword":["BERT model analysis","Model compression techniques","Neural network overparameterization","Training objective modifications","Transformer-based models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9701D20978AFABA0B786D1939C02DBA4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olga","key":"kovalevapau","last":"Kovaleva","name":"Kovaleva, Olga","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rumshiskypau","last":"Rumshisky","name":"Rumshisky, Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["2307387X"],"journal":"Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics","pages":"842-866","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098839172"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-40be91bf-0fd1-449e-9d0d-ac2961bdd112"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Primer in BERTology: What We Know About How BERT Works","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695236","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: To evaluate the impact in terms of use of health services, clinical outcomes, functional status, and patient’s satisfaction of an integrated care program, the CareWell program, for complex patients with multimorbidity, supported by information and communication technology platforms in six European regions. Data Sources: Primary data were used and the follow-up period ranged between 8 and 12 months. Study design: A quasi-experimental study, targeting chronic patients aged 65 or older, with 2 or more conditions - one of them necessarily being diabetes, congestive heart failure or congestive obstructive pulmonary disease. The intervention group received the integrated care program and the control group received usual care. Generalized mixed regression models were used. Data collection: Data were obtained from individual interviews and electronic clinical records. Principal Findings: Overall, 856 patients were recruited (475 intervention and 381 control). In the intervention group, the number of visits to emergency rooms was significantly lower, and the number of visits to the general practitioners and primary care nurses was higher than in the control group. Conclusion: The CareWell program resulted in improvements in the use of health services, strengthening the role of PC as the cornerstone of care provision for complex patients with multimorbidity.","author_count":43,"contributors":["Mateo-Abad, Maider","Fullaondo, Ane","Merino, Marisa","Gris, Stefano","Marchet, Francesco","Avolio, Francesca","Graps, Elisabetta Anna","Ravic, Mario","Kovac, Mario","Benkovic, Vanesa","Stevanovic, Ranko","Zwiefka, Antoni","Davies, Daniel","Mancin, Silvia","Forestiero, Antonella","Stafylas, Panos","Hurtado, Mayte","d’Angelantonio, Marco","Daugbjerg, Signe","Pedersen, Claus Duedal","Hammerschmidt, Reinhard","Stroetmann, Veli","Azkargorta, Lierni","Giné, Anna","Verdoy, Dolores","Soto-Gordoa, Myriam","Mora, Joana","Mar, Javier","Vergara, Itziar","De Manuel Keenoy, Esteban","De Manuel, Esteban","Merino, Maria Luisa","Faria, Angel","Stafylas, Panagiotis","D’Angelantonio, Marco","Hurtado, Maite","Dragic, Leon","Gustin, Karlo","Dario, Claudio","Saccavini, Claudio","Green, Ian","Rogers, Andrew","Summerfield, Tanya","Lewis, Leo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-636890"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["The CareWell project group"],"corresponding_author":["Mateo-Abad, Maider"],"country":["Belgium","Croatia","Germany","Greece","Ireland","Italy","Poland","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Agenzia Regionale per la salute e Sociale - Regione Puglia","All Global Affiliations","Arsenàl.IT","Biodonostia Health Research Institute","Croatian Society for Pharmacoeconomics and Health Economics","Empirica Communication and Technology Research","Ericsson Nikola Tesla d d","HealThink","Health Information Management SA","Health Services Research on Chronic Patients Network (REDISSEC)","International Foundation for Integrated Care","Kronikgune","Kronikgune Institute for Health Services Research","LSV Marshal Office","Local Health Authority","Mondragon","Powys Teaching Health Board","Regional Strategic Agency for Health and Social Affair (AReSS)","Tolosaldea Integrated Health Care Organization","University of Zagreb"],"keyword":["Elderly","ICT","Integrated care","Multimorbidity","Patient empowerment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact assessment of an innovative integrated care model for older complex patients with multimorbidity the carewell project","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5334/ijic.4711","version":"Published 