ine M.","rank":95,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 42","corresponding":null,"first":"Hannah P.","key":"wilsonpau","last":"Wilson","name":"Wilson, Hannah P.","rank":96,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 29","corresponding":null,"first":"John R.I.","key":"woodpau","last":"Wood","name":"Wood, John R.I.","rank":97,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17","corresponding":null,"first":"Li Bing","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Li Bing","rank":98,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 43","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter C.","key":"vanwelzenpau","last":"van Welzen","name":"van Welzen, Peter C.","rank":99,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32760001"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-020-2549-5","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7822","journal":"Nature","pages":"579-583","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"584"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089022059"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-17110391-d790-4083-98e3-0ccfd5e71553"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"New Guinea has the world’s richest island flora","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-142652","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Much of the recent success in NLP is due to the large Transformer-based models such as BERT (Devlin et al, 2019). However, these models have been shown to be reducible to a smaller number of self-attention heads and layers. We consider this phenomenon from the perspective of the lottery ticket hypothesis. For fine-tuned BERT, we show that (a) it is possible to find a subnetwork of elements that achieves performance comparable with that of the full model, and (b) similarly-sized subnetworks sampled from the rest of the model perform worse. However, the \"bad\" subnetworks can be fine-tuned separately to achieve only slightly worse performance than the \"good\" ones, indicating that most weights in the pre-trained BERT are potentially useful. We also show that the \"good\" subnetworks vary considerably across GLUE tasks, opening up the possibilities to learn what knowledge BERT actually uses at inference time.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Prasanna, Sai","Rogers, Anna","Rumshisky, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695293"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","OECD"],"country":["India","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Massachusetts","Zoho"],"keyword":["BERT Fine tuning","Lottery Ticket Hypothesis","Natural Language Processing","Self attention heads","Subnetwork performance","Transformer models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"when bert plays the lottery all tickets are winning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85102547740","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695293","identifier":[{"id":"85102547740","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c60fe9da-90b2-4321-b32a-5a3a66b50765"],"keyword":["BERT Fine-tuning","Lottery Ticket Hypothesis","Natural Language Processing","Self-attention heads","Subnetwork performance","Transformer models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A7BD382F2C22F36AD9A02D166A1A761D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"zoho","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Zoho","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sai","key":"prasannapau","last":"Prasanna","name":"Prasanna, Sai","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rumshiskypau","last":"Rumshisky","name":"Rumshisky, Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"3208-3229","place":"Online","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of EMNLP"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c60fe9da-90b2-4321-b32a-5a3a66b50765"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"When BERT Plays the Lottery, All Tickets Are Winning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695293","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
