{"abstract":"This paper presents RuSentiment, a new dataset for sentiment analysis of social media posts in Russian, and a new set of comprehensive annotation guidelines that are extensible to other languages. RuSentiment is currently the largest in its class for Russian, with 31,185 posts annotated with Fleiss’ kappa of 0.58 (3 annotations per post). To diversify the dataset, 6,950 posts were pre-selected with an active learning-style strategy. We report baseline classification results, and we also release the best-performing embeddings trained on 3.2B tokens of Russian VKontakte posts.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Romanov, Alexey","Rumshisky, Anna","Volkova, Svitlana","Gronas, Mikhail","Gribov, Alex"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695299"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dartmouth College","Pacific Northwest National Laboratory","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["Annotation Guidelines","RuSentiment dataset","Russian language","Sentiment analysis","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rusentiment an enriched sentiment analysis dataset for social media in russian","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85109473655","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695299","identifier":[{"id":"85109473655","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d758e944-41f5-488a-94cf-dc9830faed49"],"keyword":["RuSentiment dataset","Russian language","annotation guidelines","sentiment analysis","social media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-958BD7701CFF0B43D5E45660EDEB641E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"pacific northwest national laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Pacific Northwest National Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"dartmouth college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Dartmouth College","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexey","key":"romanovpau","last":"Romanov","name":"Romanov, Alexey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rumshiskypau","last":"Rumshisky","name":"Rumshisky, Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Svitlana","key":"volkovapau","last":"Volkova","name":"Volkova, Svitlana","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikhail","key":"gronaspau","last":"Gronas","name":"Gronas, Mikhail","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alex","key":"gribovpau","last":"Gribov","name":"Gribov, Alex","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"755-763","place":"Santa Fe, New Mexico, USA","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 27th International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d758e944-41f5-488a-94cf-dc9830faed49"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RuSentiment: An Enriched Sentiment Analysis Dataset for Social Media in Russian","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695299","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Languages with logographic writing systems present a difficulty for traditional character-level models. Leveraging the subcharacter information was recently shown to be beneficial for a number of intrinsic and extrinsic tasks in Chinese. We examine whether the same strategies could be applied for Japanese, and contribute a new analogy dataset for this language.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Karpinska, Marzena","Li, Bofang","Rogers, Anna","Drozd, Aleksandr"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695290"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","Japan"],"glorg":["AIST- Tokyo Tech Real World Big-Data Computation Open Innovation Laboratory","All Global Affiliations","Renmin University of China","The University of Tokyo","Tokyo Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Character level models","Chinese language processing","Japanese language analogies","Logographic writing systems","Subcharacter information"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subcharacter information in japanese embeddings when is it worth it","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/W18-2905","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695290","ids":["itu-c016d87e-1895-4d50-a2ff-9695b3a5536e"],"keyword":["Character-level models","Chinese language processing","Japanese language analogies","Logographic writing systems","Subcharacter information"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1124B5795053A155125A9B26B8D0B554"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"jp","key":"the university of tokyo","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"The University of Tokyo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"renmin university of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Renmin University of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"tokyo institute of technology","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Tokyo Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"jp","key":"aist tokyo tech real world big data computation open innovation laboratory","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"AIST- Tokyo Tech Real World Big-Data Computation Open Innovation Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":5,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marzena","key":"karpinskapau","last":"Karpinska","name":"Karpinska, Marzena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bofang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bofang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandr","key":"drozdpau","last":"Drozd","name":"Drozd, Aleksandr","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"28-37","place":"Melbourne, Australia","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Workshop on the Relevance of Linguistic Structure in Neural Architectures for NLP"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c016d87e-1895-4d50-a2ff-9695b3a5536e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Subcharacter Information in Japanese Embeddings: When Is It Worth It?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695290","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Attempts to find a single technique for general-purpose intrinsic evaluation of word embeddings have so far not been successful. We present a new approach based on scaled-up qualitative analysis of word vector neighborhoods that quantifies interpretable characteristics of a given model (e.g. its preference for synonyms or shared morphological forms as nearest neighbors). We analyze 21 such factors and show how they correlate with performance on 14 extrinsic and intrinsic task datasets (and also explain the lack of correlation between some of them). Our approach enables multi-faceted evaluation, parameter search, and generally – a more principled, hypothesis-driven approach to development of distributional semantic representations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Hosur Ananthakrishna, Shashwath","Rumshisky, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695266"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Massachusetts"],"keyword":["Correlation analysis","Intrinsic Evaluation","Qualitative analysis","Semantic Representation","Word Embeddings"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what s in your embedding and how it predicts task performance","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/C18-1228","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695266","ids":["itu-937a9c98-041c-4106-b22f-3a1c62abd91a"],"keyword":["Correlation Analysis","Intrinsic Evaluation","Qualitative Analysis","Semantic Representation","Word Embeddings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FDDB4C02594A66E16AA4FED0CA10DDE2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of massachusetts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Massachusetts","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Shashwath","key":"hosurananthakrishnapau","last":"Hosur Ananthakrishna","name":"Hosur Ananthakrishna, Shashwath","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rumshiskypau","last":"Rumshisky","name":"Rumshisky, Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"2690-2703","place":"Santa Fe, New Mexico, USA, August 20-26, 2018","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 27th International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-937a9c98-041c-4106-b22f-3a1c62abd91a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What's in Your Embedding, And How It Predicts Task Performance","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695266","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The prevalence and spectrum of germline mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2 have been reported in single populations, with the majority of reports focused on White in Europe and North America. The Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) has assembled data on 18,435 families with BRCA1 mutations and 11,351 families with BRCA2 mutations ascertained from 69 centers in 49 countries on six continents. This study comprehensively describes the characteristics of the 1,650 unique BRCA1 and 1,731 unique BRCA2 deleterious (disease-associated) mutations identified in the CIMBA database. We observed substantial variation in mutation type and frequency by geographical region and race/ethnicity. In addition to known founder mutations, mutations of relatively high frequency were identified in specific racial/ethnic or geographic groups that may reflect founder mutations and which could be used in targeted (panel) first pass genotyping for specific populations. Knowledge of the population-specific mutational spectrum in BRCA1 and BRCA2 could inform efficient strategies for genetic testing and may justify a more broad-based oncogenetic testing in some populations.","author_count":241,"contributors":["Rebbeck, Timothy R","Friebel, Tara M","Friedman, Eitan","Hamann, Ute","Huo, Dezheng","Kwong, Ava","Olah, Edith","Olopade, Olufunmilayo I","Solano, Angela R","Teo, Soo-Hwang","Thomassen, Mads","Weitzel, Jeffrey N","Chan, T L","Couch, Fergus J","Goldgar, David E","Kruse, Torben A","Palmero, Edenir Inêz","Park, Sue Kyung","Torres, Diana","van Rensburg, Elizabeth J","McGuffog, Lesley","Parsons, Michael T","Leslie, Goska","Aalfs, Cora M","Abugattas, Julio","Adlard, Julian","Agata, Simona","Aittomäki, Kristiina","Andrews, Lesley","Andrulis, Irene L","Arason, Adalgeir","Arnold, Norbert","Arun, Banu K","Asseryanis, Ella","Auerbach, Leo","Azzollini, Jacopo","Balmaña, Judith","Barile, Monica","Barkardottir, Rosa B","Barrowdale, Daniel","Benitez, Javier","Berger, Andreas"