{"abstract":"This paper explores the possibilities of analogical reasoning with vector space models. Given two pairs of words with the same relation (e.g. man:woman :: king:queen), it was proposed that the offset between one pair of the corresponding word vectors can be used to identify the unknown member of the other pair (king - man + woman = queen). We argue against such “linguistic regularities” as a model for linguistic relations in vector space models and as a benchmark, and we show that the vector offset (as well as two other, better-performing methods) suffers from dependence on vector similarity.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rogers, Anna","Drozd, Aleksandr","Li, Bofang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695246"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Renmin University of China","Tokyo Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Analogical reasoning","Linguistic Relations","Vector Similarity","Vector Space Models","Word Vectors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the too many problems of analogical reasoning with word vectors","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85036662540","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695246","identifier":[{"id":"85036662540","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5b74302a-8842-4418-99d8-f67b7cf0edb3"],"keyword":["Analogical Reasoning","Linguistic Relations","Vector Similarity","Vector Space Models","Word Vectors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DDF2AA708F6D8EBAEA771827343B5254"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"jp","key":"tokyo institute of technology","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Tokyo Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"renmin university of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Renmin University of China","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandr","key":"drozdpau","last":"Drozd","name":"Drozd, Aleksandr","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bofang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bofang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"135-148","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 6th Joint Conference on Lexical and Computational Semantics (* SEM 2017)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5b74302a-8842-4418-99d8-f67b7cf0edb3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The (Too Many) Problems of Analogical Reasoning with Word Vectors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695246","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The number of word embedding models is growing every year. Most of them are based on the co-occurrence information of words and their contexts. However, it is still an open question what is the best definition of context. We provide a systematical investigation of 4 different syntactic context types and context representations for learning word embeddings. Comprehensive experiments are conducted to evaluate their effectiveness on 6 extrinsic and intrinsic tasks. We hope that this paper, along with the published code, would be helpful for choosing the best context type and representation for a given task.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Li, Bofang","Liu, Tao","Zhao, Zhe","Tang, Buzhou","Drozd, Aleksandr","Rogers, Anna","Du, Xiaoyong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695313"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harbin Institute of Technology","Renmin University of China","Tokyo Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Co occurrence Information","Context Representations","Extrinsic and Intrinsic Evaluation","Syntactic Context Types","Word Embedding Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating different syntactic context types and context representations for learning word embeddings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://aclweb.org/anthology/D17-1257","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695313","ids":["itu-fe14e6a2-e70f-4b28-ac39-4d5e1099334d"],"keyword":["Co-occurrence Information","Context Representations","Extrinsic and Intrinsic Evaluation","Syntactic Context Types","Word Embedding Models"],"lang":"English","le